329
01:01:16,724 --> 01:01:31,764
Compression is a process of transforming data to code sets functioned to reduce the usage of memory, whether or not by reducing data quality and accelerating data transmission time.

330
01:01:32,443 --> 01:01:42,563
The data can be text, picture, audio and video. Many algorithms can be used to compress data. It can be classified into two classes.

331
01:01:43,315 --> 01:01:46,315
LoseLess ve LoseLess.

332
01:01:46,315 --> 01:01:57,227
Textfiles are still dominant to be used in many storage devices, including mobile storage device,

333
01:01:57,652 --> 01:02:25,516
Bu, bu

334
01:02:25,780 --> 01:02:31,820
Tradition. The writer's application will be the case study of the research paper.

335
01:02:33,140 --> 01:02:42,780
Mythology. There are four scheme combination of three algorithms that will be conducted in this research paper.

336
01:02:43,572 --> 01:03:07,212
Örneğe, Scheme 1 will only adapt arythmatic coding. Scheme 2 will function move to front code and arithmetic coding. Scheme 3 will employ Burroughs-Willer transform and arithmetic coding without move to front. Scheme 4 will use the Burroughs-Willer transform, move to front code and arithmetic coding.

337
01:03:08,332 --> 01:03:10,212
Arithmetic coding

338
01:03:11,347 --> 01:03:24,147
Bypasses the idea of replacing an input symbol with specific code. It replaces the sequences of symbols in the input file with single arithmetic number.

339
01:03:24,147 --> 01:03:30,347
More longer input messages, more bits are needed in the arithmetic number.

340
01:03:32,307 --> 01:03:40,368
An arithmetik coding process is a single number less than 1 and greater than or equal to 0.

341
01:03:41,619 --> 01:03:50,259
Arithmetic Coding, its single number can be uniquely decoded to create the exact stream of symbols.

342
01:03:50,259 --> 01:03:56,900
To construct the output number, the symbols are assigned to set of probabilities.

343
01:03:57,559 --> 01:04:07,339
Each character is assigned the portion of the 0 to 1 range that corresponds to its probability of appearance.

344
01:04:08,244 --> 01:04:18,744
Move to Front Code. Move to Front Code is the transformed algorithm that does not compress data but can help to reduce redundancy.

345
01:04:18,744 --> 01:04:29,744
The main idea is that each symbol in the data is replaced by its index in the stack of recently used symbols.

346
01:04:30,867 --> 01:04:45,667
Long sequences of identical symbols will be replaced by zeros, whereas symbol that don't appear in a long time will be replaced by large number.

347
01:04:45,667 --> 01:04:47,067
Thus,

348
01:04:47,443 --> 01:05:02,403
At the end of the data is transformed into a sequence of integers. If the data exhibits a lot of local correlation, then these integers tend to be small.

349
01:05:03,411 --> 01:05:25,371
Burroughs-Wheeler Transform. The Burroughs and Wheeler Transform BWT is a block sorting loseless transform. BWT was invented in 1983 and published as Teknikal Report in 1994 by Michael Burroughs and David Wheeler.

350
01:05:26,036 --> 01:05:33,436
BWT can permute a text into a new sequence which is usually more compressible.

351
01:05:33,436 --> 01:05:45,436
The remarkable thing about BWT is not only that it generates more easily compressible output, but also that is reversible.

352
01:06:10,420 --> 01:06:36,600
